          <h1 id="warranty-title">Warranty Policy</h1>
          <p class="lead">This page explains manufacturer and JOOD warranty coverage, claim steps, repair & replacement procedures, and important exclusions for products purchased from our store.</p>
          <p class="muted-small"><strong>Effective date:</strong> 1 January 2026 — <strong>Last updated:</strong> February 13, 2026</p>
        </div>

        <div class="hero-media" aria-hidden="true">
          <img src="/customer/images/warranty/warranty-hero.png" alt="Warranty and service illustration">
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- POLICY CONTENT -->
    <section aria-label="Warranty policy">
      <div class="grid">
        <div>
          <article class="card" aria-labelledby="warranty-heading">
            <h2 id="warranty-heading">Overview</h2>
            <p class="muted">Our warranty framework consists of (A) manufacturer warranties provided by the product maker, and (B) JOOD's limited warranty where specified. This policy explains how to identify coverage, make a claim, and the remedies available (repair, replacement, or refund).</p>

            <h3 id="coverage">What the warranty covers</h3>
            <p class="muted">Subject to the conditions below, warranty coverage may include:</p>
            <ul class="value-list muted">
              <li>Manufacturing defects in materials or workmanship discovered within the warranty period.</li>
              <li>Functional failures under normal use as described in product documentation.</li>
              <li>Included manufacturer service plans (if clearly stated on the product page or packaging).</li>
            </ul>

            <h3 id="warranty-period">Warranty period & how to find it</h3>
            <p class="muted">Warranty length varies by product and manufacturer. Typical examples:</p>
            <ul class="value-list muted">
              <li>Electronics: 12–24 months depending on manufacturer specifications.</li>
              <li>Small appliances: 12 months from date of purchase unless stated otherwise.</li>
              <li>Consumables and accessories: warranty periods are typically shorter or limited to defects on delivery.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="muted">To find the exact warranty for your purchase: check the product page, the included warranty card/documentation, or the original invoice/receipt.</p>

            <h3 id="exclusions">What is NOT covered</h3>
            <p class="muted">Warranty does not cover:</p>
            <ul class="value-list muted">
              <li>Damage caused by misuse, abuse, negligence, improper installation, or non-commercial use outside of stated instructions.</li>
              <li>Accidental damage, cosmetic damage (scratches, dents), and wear and tear from normal use.</li>
              <li>Damage caused by unauthorised repair, modification or use of non-approved parts/accessories.</li>
              <li>Consumables (batteries, filters, bulbs) unless expressly covered.</li>
              <li>Loss, theft, or damage from external factors (water, fire, power surges) unless specifically included in a warranty endorsement.</li>
            </ul>

            <h3 id="proof">Proof of purchase & obligations</h3>
            <p class="muted">Claims require proof of purchase (order number or invoice) and, where relevant, photos or video showing the issue. Keep original packaging and accessories when possible to aid diagnostics.</p>

            <h3 id="how-to-claim">How to make a warranty claim</h3>
            <ol class="value-list muted">
              <li>Contact JOOD Support: use <a href="/customer/support-and-help/contact-us">Contact Us</a> or open a ticket from your account (My Orders &rarr; Request support) with order details and evidence (photos/video).</li>
              <li>Our support team will triage the request and provide instructions — you may be asked to run simple diagnostics or upload additional information.</li>
              <li>If authorised, you will receive a return authorisation and shipping instructions (prepaid label for covered faults where JOOD or the manufacturer accepts liability).</li>
              <li>Returned items will be inspected by our technicians or the manufacturer; outcomes can include repair, replacement, refund or a repair quote if outside warranty.</li>
            </ol>

            <h3 id="repair-replace">Repair, replacement & refunds</h3>
            <p class="muted">Where a valid warranty claim is accepted:</p>
            <ul class="value-list muted">
              <li><strong>Repair</strong> — the item will be repaired and returned to you; turnaround depends on part availability and diagnostics.</li>
              <li><strong>Replacement</strong> — if the item cannot be repaired, we will replace it with the same model or a comparable model of equal value.</li>
              <li><strong>Refund</strong> — where repair/replacement is impractical, we may offer a refund to the original payment method. Refund amounts may be adjusted for use where permitted by law.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="muted">JOOD or the manufacturer will cover reasonable shipping costs for accepted warranty claims. For claims outside warranty or change-of-mind returns, shipping may be customer-paid.</p>

            <h3 id="third-party">Third-party & extended warranties</h3>
            <p class="muted">Some products include or offer extended warranty packages from third-party providers. These are governed by the third-party contract — contact the provider directly for service under extended plans. JOOD can assist with escalations where we facilitated the sale.</p>

            <h3 id="unauthorised">Unauthorised repairs & voiding</h3>
            <p class="muted">Unauthorized repair attempts, tampering, or using non-approved parts may void the warranty. Always follow the manufacturer’s guidance and obtain authorisation through JOOD Support before sending items for service.</p>

            <h3 id="international">International purchases & warranty transfer</h3>
            <p class="muted">Warranty coverage may be regional. For cross-border purchases, warranty terms (and eligible service centres) depend on the manufacturer’s international warranty policy. Contact support for guidance when shipping items internationally for service.</p>

            <h3 id="timelines">Estimated timelines</h3>
            <p class="muted">Turnaround times vary by product and fault complexity. Typical estimates after an authorised return is received:</p>
            <ul class="value-list muted">
              <li>Initial inspection & diagnostics: 3–7 business days</li>
              <li>Repair or parts replacement: 7–21 business days depending on availability</li>
              <li>Replacement dispatch: 3–7 business days after approval</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="muted">These are estimates — we will provide more accurate timelines during the claim process.</p>

            <h3 id="escalation">Escalation & dispute resolution</h3>
            <p class="muted">If you are unsatisfied with the outcome, please escalate to our Returns & Warranty Manager via support. For unresolved disputes, customers may pursue local consumer protection channels or dispute resolution mechanisms applicable in their jurisdiction.</p>

            <h3 id="consumer-rights">Consumer rights & legal notes</h3>
            <p class="muted">This policy is in addition to, and does not limit, your statutory consumer rights. Where local law provides stronger protections (for example, implied guarantees), those rights will apply.</p>

            <h2 id="contact">Contact & service locations</h2>
            <p class="muted">For warranty claims and service enquiries:</p>
            <div class="muted" style="margin-top:10px">
              <p><strong>Support email:</strong> <a href="mailto:support@jood.com">support@jood.com</a></p>
              <p><strong>Phone:</strong> +971-55-555-5555</p>
              <p><strong>Service address:</strong> 13th Floor, Al Reem Tower, Dubai, UAE</p>
            </div>

            <p class="note">This Warranty Policy sets operational expectations and is not a contract of insurance. For contract-level warranty obligations, manufacturer terms govern. If you need a printable or plain-text legal copy, we can prepare one for record-keeping.</p>
          </article>
        </div>

